; Whether the generated relabel rules keep and drop the containers they mean to
; is a question only Alloy can answer: the rules name labels, and which labels
; exist is decided by Alloy's Docker discovery, not by this tree. A test that
; reads the generated text agrees with whatever the generator wrote, including
; a rule over a label nothing produces. So the script runs the real image
; against real labelled containers and reads what its components computed.
;
; The verdict is the script's exit code, as for test/ssh_real_sshd: it must skip
; where Docker is absent and fail where Docker was expected, and neither is
; expressible as a snapshot.

; A private probe: no public name and no package, so nothing installs it and
; nothing but the rule below builds or runs it.

(executable
 (name emit_config)
 (modules emit_config)
 (libraries bondi.common))

; CI is named rather than inherited, so a run that skipped for want of Docker is
; not the cached answer to a run that must fail because CI is set.

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (deps
  (:script alloy_real_docker.sh))
 (action
  (setenv
   CI
   %{env:CI=}
   (run bash %{script} %{exe:emit_config.exe}))))
